      "text": "Consider the given Functional dependencies.\nFor a Relation R(ABCDE):\nA → B\nB → C\nBC → A\nA → D\nE → A\nD → E\nWhich of the following is not a key?",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "B"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "C"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "D"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "E"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "B",
      "correctText": "C",
      "explanation": "A → B\nB → C\nBC → A\nA → D\nE → A\nD → E\n\nA+ = {ABCDE}\nB+ = {BCADE}\nC+ = {C}\nD+ = {DEABC}\nE+ = {EABCD}\n∴ ‘C’ is not the key.\nChoice (B)",
      "status": "confirmed",
      "image": "images/Databases_4/databases_4-q013-explanation.png"
    },
